    "topic": "Coronary",
    "stem": "<p>A 71-year-old woman with severe aortic stenosis and marked concentric LV hypertrophy undergoes induction of general anesthesia. Her heart rate rises from 65 to 105 bpm and her blood pressure falls from 130/75 to 90/50 mmHg. Which physiological explanation best accounts for why this combination is especially dangerous in her specific case?</p>",
